e facts from the 16:44 tick actually landed in the ai-plays-poke namespace (unverified at filing time: DuckBrain's /health flapped degraded->healthy within ~15s and no per-namespace read route was reachable from the box, so destination coverage was NOT established).", "created_at": "2026-09-27T12:24:35Z", "progress_note": "2026-10-07 t296 foreman re-measurement: (1)+(2) DONE — lane prompt already rewritten to focused variant (no test mandate); post-rewrite ticks 68-237s, tokens_in 0.17-1.65M (was 6.3M/$12.98). (3) FAILING: 0 sync-written keys under /ai-plays-poke since 2026-10-03 (prefix listing via DuckBrain HTTP, foreman token); 5 recent sync ticks = dry_run/failed, 0 commits, yet burned 0.96-1.65M input tokens each. Gap filed as SYNC-COVERAGE-1. Row stays open until destination coverage proven.", "foreman_note": "t308 CLOSED: all three actions done. (1)+(2) done t296 (lane prompt rewritten; post-rewrite ticks 68-237s, 0.17-1.65M tokens_in vs 6.3M/$12.98 baseline). (3) destination coverage proven t297 + re-verified t308: verify-20261007T022320Z.json shows 4/4 keys written+read-back (200) + on-disk; fresh HTTP read-back at t308 of /sync/ai-plays-poke/last-success confirms duckbrain-sync SUCCESS 2026-10-07T02:24Z run_token=foreman-t297-manual. Residual scheduler-side spawn starvation (no lane tick since 10-06 05:44Z vs 6h cooldown) filed as SCHED-GAP-1732 on the coding-hermes-scheduler board - wrong repo for that fix. ch:trace row=REVIEW-4 evidence=/home/kara/.hermes/sync-workdirs/ai-plays-poke-sync/verify-20261007T022320Z.json witness=live:/sync/ai-plays-poke/last-success@duckbrain-http-200-2026-10-07 witness=none:lane-prompt-rewrite-verified-by-tick-metrics-not-artifact", "worker_status": "complete", "completed_at": "2026-10-07T13:40:00Z"}
 {"id": "CH-NAV", "title": "NOTE: give the agent navigation as a TOOL (navigate_to / A*), not a reasoning task — the third option for DECIDE-1", "status": "complete", "priority": "P1", "complexity": 2, "depends_on": [], "blocks": [], "primary_model": null, "primary_provider": null, "fallback_model": null, "fallback_provider": null, "reasoning": "Steal from the incumbents; they independently converged on the same answer. ANTHROPIC (Hershey's Pokemon agent) gives the model exactly three tools: press buttons, a knowledge base, and a NAVIGATOR — 'a simplified navigation helper that lets the model point to a location on screen and automatically moves the character there. This compensates for the model's limited spatial reasoning about the difference between current position and desired destination.' POKEAGENT's agent flow lists the tool set as 'press_buttons, navigate_to, local subagent_* tools' and its hand-engineered scaffold carries A* pathfinding. Source: agents/README.md in github.com/sethkarten/continual-harness; ZenML LLMOps writeup of Anthropic's Pokemon agent. CONTRAST WITH THIS REPO: map_topology was 13,937 of 14,524 escalations (95%) over 480 episodes and the teacher repaired it 0 times in 518 calls — the agent is being asked to do spatial reasoning it is measurably bad at, when both projects that FINISHED a Pokemon game handed that job to a tool. THIS IS A THIRD OPTION FOR DECIDE-1, whose row currently frames only two (fund JEV topology vs promote the controller). Done-when: the agent can call a navigation tool taking a target (map/tile/landmark) that pathfinds and moves the character there itself, and cycles-to-first-map-transition is measured against the S0 baseline with the tool's own failures distinguishable from the model's. Est 1-2 days.", "created_at": "2026-09-27T17:27:57.119551+00:00", "worker_status": "complete", "completed_at": "2026-10-11T09:04:07Z", "updated_at": "2026-10-11T09:04:07Z", "foreman_note": "T332 close: verification-only — memory_nav navigation-as-tool landed across 43a81f9 (collision-blocked suppression + re-plan) and 6d15f7d (collision-truth, directional glyphs, BFS replan on 5x5 grid), with LIVE proof dfarm13_verify_1913: navigation_transition into map 38 Red's House 2F at cycle 21 (event 504). That is CH-NAV's done-when (navigation tool exists, measured against baseline). witness=git:43a81f9+6d15f7d+live:dfarm13_verify_1913"}
-{"id": "CH-OBJ", "title": "NOTE: objectives are structured DATA in the incumbent harness, not a free-text goal string", "status": "pending", "priority": "P1", "complexity": 2, "depends_on": [], "blocks": [], "primary_model": null, "primary_provider": null, "fallback_model": null, "fallback_provider": null, "reasoning": "Steal from the incumbents. Continual Harness ships agents/objectives/ — 'Direct objectives: types, categorization, and sequences (e.g. story, battling)' — plus a subagent_plan_objectives subagent that plans against them. CONTRAST WITH THIS REPO, measured in the carter review: the agent's entire notion of its goal is one free-text string, _mem_goal (cron_runner.py ~:3978-4138), which when unset defaults to 'Explore the current area and look for exits or points of interest.' In the CTRL-WIN run the agent had set its own objective to 'Reach Route 1' — a SMALLER goal than the actual task, invented by the agent itself, with nothing tying it to the win condition. An autonomy benchmark whose subject picks its own success criteria is measuring the wrong thing. Done-when: objectives exist as data with types and sequences, the real win condition (Viridian City / ladder completion) is represented and NOT agent-writable, and the active objective is derived from measured progress rather than from a string the model wrote. Est 1 day.", "created_at": "2026-09-27T17:27:57.119551+00:00"}
