 {"id": "CH-SPLIT", "title": "NOTE: split the environment from the agent — game+emulator as a server, agent as a client", "status": "complete", "priority": "P2", "complexity": 3, "depends_on": [], "blocks": [], "primary_model": null, "primary_provider": null, "fallback_model": null, "fallback_provider": null, "reasoning": "Steal from the incumbents. Continual Harness 'uses a headless server: the game and emulator run in a server process; agents and UIs run as clients. The server exposes HTTP REST endpoints and POST /mcp/* routes; clients poll for state and submit actions.' That separation is what makes their scaffold comparison possible at all — the same environment is driven by `continualharness`, `pokeagent`, `simple`, and `simplest` scaffolds. CONTRAST WITH THIS REPO: the loop, the prompts, the memory writes and the decision gate all live in one 5,586-line cron_runner.py, so the agent cannot be swapped without editing the environment. This is also the enabling change for CH-MCP and CH-SUBA. Done-when: the emulator + RAM reader are reachable as a service with a documented observe/act contract, and at least one agent implementation that is NOT cron_runner.py drives the same environment to a measured milestone. Est 3-5 days.", "created_at": "2026-09-27T17:27:57.119551+00:00", "worker_status": "complete", "commit_hash": "4316983", "completed_at": "2026-10-08 03:05:00", "foreman_note": "T322: increment 1 landed — FastAPI env service (boot/observe/act/reset/health) + example client + contract doc + 12 tests. Commit 4316983 pushed, guard 5/5 full, T4 smoke Pallet Town via RAM. Row kept open-as-new-scope: non-cron_runner agent milestone (CH-SUBA/CH-MCP enabling) still pending; re-file increment 2 rows as needed.", "worker_summary": "Worker glm-5.3-flash@xkiro authored all 4 artifacts, exited 130 pre-commit; foreman completed commit + gates.", "guard_result": "tier1 5/5 FULL; pytest env_service 12p; assist-inventory guard green after declaring /env/act site"}
 {"id": "CH-SUBA", "title": "NOTE: subagents as callable tools (battler / planner / reflect / verify / summarize) — the reference design for DELEG-1", "status": "pending", "priority": "P2", "complexity": 2, "depends_on": [], "blocks": [], "primary_model": null, "primary_provider": null, "fallback_model": null, "fallback_provider": null, "reasoning": "Steal from the incumbents. Continual Harness ships a local subagent library exposed to the orchestrator as tools: subagent_reflect, subagent_verify, subagent_gym_puzzle, subagent_summarize, subagent_battler, subagent_plan_objectives (agents/subagents/), with shared plumbing in subagents/utils/ (registry, runtime, context, trajectory_window). Their looping subagents 'consume real global steps per inner turn but only return compacted summaries/results to the orchestrator's short-term memory'. CONTRAST WITH THIS REPO: delegation is absent entirely — this is S5/DELEG-1, still pending, with no subagent of any kind. CH-SUBA is the concrete reference shape for it. Done-when: >=1 subagent callable as a tool whose returned finding is written to memory and consumed in a later cycle (DELEG-1's own acceptance), with the subagent's inner steps not flooding the orchestrator's context. Est 2-3 days. Blocks DELEG-1.", "created_at": "2026-09-27T17:27:57.119551+00:00"}
 {"id": "CH-CTX", "title": "NOTE: the incumbent harness manages its context window — cap turns, compact via subagents; ours is 6 notes / 300 chars", "status": "pending", "priority": "P2", "complexity": 2, "depends_on": [], "blocks": [], "primary_model": null, "primary_provider": null, "fallback_model": null, "fallback_provider": null, "reasoning": "Steal from the incumbents, and note this is CTX-WIN's missing half. Continual Harness caps the orchestrator's short-term memory at 20 TURNS and has looping subagents return compacted summaries so inner steps do not consume the window; its checkpoints restore disk state (objectives, long-term memory, trajectories) rather than an in-memory conversation. CONTRAST WITH THIS REPO, measured: the decision path is a fresh two-message request every cycle (cron_runner.py:2115, messages=[{system},{user}] and nothing else); what survives between cycles is _mem_notes capped at 6 entries joined and truncated to 300 characters, plus one _mem_goal string (cron_runner.py:~4502). Prior turns reach the TEACHER request only (cron_runner.py:1409). CTX-WIN is marked complete but its judge verdict was INCOMPLETE on input budget, so treat it as unverified and this as the reference implementation. Done-when: the decision request carries a bounded, managed window of prior turns (with a compaction path for older ones) and the agent can answer a question about a cycle >N back. Est 2 days.", "created_at": "2026-09-27T17:27:57.119551+00:00"}
